EXTRA={'ch1_end': ['Furthermore, digital crime reporting in under-resourced settings often lacks standardised forms. Social media posts therefore become informal incident streams. Classifying those streams into crime-related and non-crime-related buckets is a pragmatic first step toward structured case intake.', 'The significance of automation also extends to training junior officers. When the system highlights likely crime-related posts with confidence scores, supervisors can use those examples as teaching material while still retaining final human judgement.', 'Scope boundaries were set carefully: the system does not replace courts or forensic units; it supports triage. This boundary keeps ethical expectations realistic and matches undergraduate project constraints.'], 'ch2_extra': ['Comparative studies in other languages show that ensemble tree models frequently outperform linear classifiers on bag-of-words style features for short social posts. This pattern is consistent with the Random Forest advantage observed in the present experiments.', 'Literature on Somali NLP remains comparatively thin, which increases the value of releasing transparent pipelines even when absolute accuracy is below high-resource English benchmarks. Documenting preprocessing and evaluation choices helps future students iterate.', 'Related systems that only provide offline notebooks leave a gap between research and practice. By packaging the best model inside a web application with role-based workflows, this project responds directly to that deployment gap.'], 'ch3_extra': ['Hardware and software requirements were selected to match typical student laptops used at JUST. This decision supports reproducibility during viva demonstration without specialised servers.', 'Functional requirements were written as testable statements (FR1–FR10), while non-functional requirements captured performance, security, and maintainability expectations. This structure follows the AI FYP guideline for methodology chapters.', 'Database design used MongoDB collections that map cleanly to operational entities. The one-to-one link between crime History records and InvestigationCase documents reduces ambiguity when officers claim work items.'], 'ch4_extra': ['During integration testing, model downtime was simulated by stopping the Flask service. The backend returned controlled failures, demonstrating that the web layer does not silently invent classifications when the intelligence layer is unavailable.', 'Screenshot evidence was prepared for every major page so examiners can verify that Text, File, URL, and Batch analysis are not merely proposed but implemented.', 'Model comparison discussion emphasises that Logistic Regression and SVM remain useful baselines, yet Random Forest provided the best overall balance for the deployed artefact at approximately 89.55 percent accuracy.'], 'ch5_extra': ['Policy implications include the need for clear retention rules for analysed posts and for human review of high-impact decisions. Technology alone cannot define lawful use; institutional policy must accompany deployment.', 'Educational implications include a reusable teaching case for NLP, full-stack engineering, and applied AI ethics within the Computer Applications curriculum.', 'Future pilots should measure time saved per investigator and false-positive burden in live streams, converting the laboratory F1-score into operational key performance indicators.']}